          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            From the point of view of infinity category theory (nPOV),
            %em descent
            is the study of generalizations of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            condition on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            to presheaves with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
          %p
            More generally,
            %strong descent theory
            studies existence and (non)uniqueness of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            in a (possibly higher) category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_X
            provided some “inverse image” functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:C_X\to C_Y
            which applied to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            produces an object in some (possibly higher) category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mi α
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f^*_\alpha:C_X\to C_{Y_\alpha}\}_{\alpha\in I}
            is given. Labels
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\alpha
            are considered as labels of local regions, over which objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{Y_\alpha}
            live and the inverse image functor is considered as some sort of restriction along geometric morphism of spaces from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\alpha\to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(u)
            with additional “gluing” data
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^*(u),\xi)
            is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong descent datum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^*(u),\xi)
            is also called a descent, and it describes the property that the (higher) category of descent data in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_Y
            is equivalent to the category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
            using pseudofunctors, and in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA1"} SGA1
            using fibered categories.
          %p
            The most important case is when there is a descent (in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+higher+categories"} equivalence of higher categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            functor along every cover of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            or its higher analogue; though many cases (for example
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+in+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} descent in noncommutative algebraic geometry
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"} sheaves
            (i.e.
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} stacks
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-presheaf"} presheaves
            as those
            = succeed "-presheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            with respect to certain morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            which are to be regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            of the
            = succeed "-presheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            down to
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p More concretely
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
                is characterized as being a sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
                of the
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
                on some (small)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                every such
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategory"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategory
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
                at a collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W = \{Y \to X\}
                of morphisms which are sent to equivalences by the left adjoint of the inclusion;
            %li
              %p
                and the sheaves in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
                are precisely the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
                with respect to this collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                of morphisms, i.e. precisely those objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in PSh(S)
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)(X,A) \to PSh(S)(Y,A)
                is an isomorphism in the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} PSh(S)(Y,A)
                in the following paragraphs.
            %li
              %p
                This condition is essentially the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em descent conditon
          %p
            In concrete models for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            – notably in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            – the morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            usually come from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
          %p
            in this case the above condition becomes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} PSh(S)(colim^\Delta Y_\bullet, A)
            which is equivalent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi lim
                      %mi Δ
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} lim^\Delta PSh(S)(Y_\bullet, A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X)
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, A)
                  \:= lim^\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
                  \\,.
          %p
            And this is the form of the
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            = succeed "." do
              %strong descent condition
          %h2#descent_for_ordinary_sheaves Descent for ordinary sheaves
          %p Descent is best understood as a direct generalization of the situation for 0-stacks, i.e. ordinary sheaves, which we briefly recall in a language suitable for the following generalization.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            any small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            the category of small sets, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{PSh}(S) = [S^{op}, Set]
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            itself, and which are summarized by saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{PSh}(S)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            respecting this structure in some sense: these are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a sub-topos of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
            in that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S)\hookrightarrow PSh(S)
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          %p
            One finds that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
            of sheaves inside presheaves is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
            at morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
            called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            precisely if it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            with respect to these
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{PSh(S)}(X,A) \stackrel{Hom_{PSh(S)}(f,A)}{\to} Hom_{PSh(S)}(Y,A)
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            This locality condition is in fact the
            %em descent
            condition: the sheaf has to descend from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            down to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em descent condition
            when evaluated on morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
            which are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
          %p
            namely if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y^1 \to X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+epimorphism"} local epimorphism
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            that corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2 : Y^2 \to Y^1 \times_X Y^1
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+epimorphism"} local epimorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⇉
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Y^\bullet := (Y^2 \rightrightarrows Y^1)
          %p
            being the two canonical morphisms out of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi colim
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  colim Y^\bullet \to X
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
          %p
            (This is exercise 16.6 in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
          %p
            Therefore for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi colim
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{PSh(S)}(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Hom_{PSh(S)}(colim Y^\bullet, A)
          %p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            may be taken out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            to make this equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi lim
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{PSh(S)}(X,A)
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  lim Hom_{PSh(S)}(Y^\bullet, A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is convenient, suggestive and common to write
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(X) := Hom_{PSh(S)}(X,A)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(Y^\bullet) := Hom_{PSh(S)}(Y^\bullet,A)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            whether or not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and/or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^\bullet
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi lim
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X)
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  lim A(Y^\bullet)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the form of the condition that is most commonly called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em descent condition
          %h2#descent_for_simplicial_presheaves Descent for simplicial presheaves
          %p
            For more references and background on the following see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+for+simplicial+presheaves"} descent for simplicial presheaves
          %p
            A well-studied class of models/presentations for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            is obtained using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            on an ordinary (1-categorical)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
            be the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Recall from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            that there is the
            %em global
            and the
            %em local
            injective simplicial model structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
            which makes it a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            and that the local model structure is a (Bousfield-)localization of the global model structure.
          %p
            So in terms of simplicial presheaves the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            that we want to describe, namely
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                localization of a simplicial model category
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localization+of+a+simplicial+model+category"} ?
          %p
            Recall that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            modeled/presented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            is the full
            = succeed "-subcategory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/highertopoi.pdf#page=528"} section 6.5.2
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
            we have:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the full simplicial subcategory on fibrant-cofibrant objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
                with respect to the
                %em global
                injective model structure is (the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                realization of) the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                the full simplicial subcategory on fibrant-cofibrant objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
                with respect to the
                %em local
                injective model structure is (the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                realization of) the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{Sh}_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
                of the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Since with respect to the local or global injective model structure all objects are automatically cofibrant, this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            is the full sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            on simplicial presheaves which are fibrant with respect to the local injective model structure: these are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            in this model.
          %p
            By the general properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            there should be a class of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            – hence between injective-fibrant objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, PSh(S)]
            – such that the simplicial presheaves representing
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            with respect to these morphisms.
          %p
            The general idea of descent in this simplicial context is the precise analog of the situation for ordinary sheaves, but with ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} (co)limits
            replaced everywhere with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+quasi-categories"} (∞,1)-categorical (co)limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            amounts to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy (co)limit
          %p
            So for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            a morphism of simplicial presheaves, the condition that a simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local
            with respect to it, hence satisfies descent with respect to it, is generally that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi RHom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi RHom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi RHom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi hocolim
                            %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi holim
                            %mi n
                          %mi RHom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi holim
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  RHom(X,A)  \stackrel{}{\to} &amp; RHom(Y,A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq RHom(hocolim_n Y_n, A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq holim_n RHom(Y_n, A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =: holim_n A(Y_n)
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            is a weak equivalence, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RHom
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RHom
            denotes the corresponding
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            – for instance the ordinary simplicial hom if both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are fibrant with respect to the given model structure.
          %p
            The details on which morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            one needs to check against here have been worked out in
          %ul
            %li
              D. Dugger, S. Hollander, D. Isaksen,
              %em Hypercovers and simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p We now describe central results of that article.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in S
              an object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              regarded as a simplicial presheaf and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in [S^{op}, SSet]
              a simplicial presheaf on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              is a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
              if it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %em local acyclic fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in S
              and all diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi respectively
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^k[n]\otimes V &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\;\; respectively \;\,
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
            %p
              there exists a covering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to V\}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with respect to the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              such that for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \to V
              in that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              the pullback of the above diagram to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi respectively
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^k[n]\otimes U_i &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\;\; respectively \;\,
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verdier+site"} Verdier site
            then every such hypercover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            has a refinement by a hypercover which is cofibrant with respect to the projective global
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            we discuss are cofibrant in this sense. These are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em split hypercovers
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=29"} DHI, def. 9.1
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
              – i.e. the fibrant objects with respect to the projective model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
              – are precisely those objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
              – i.e.
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed "," do
                %strong satisfy descent for all split hypercovers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    [S^{op}, SSet](Y,A)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} weak equivalence of simplicial sets
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=3"} DHI, thm 1.3
              formulated in the light of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=9"} DHI, lemma 4.4 (ii)
          %p
            Notice that by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
            every simplicial presheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : S^{op} \to SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \Delta^{op}\times S^{op} \to Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \simeq colim^\Delta F_\bullet
          %p
            which is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \simeq \int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \cdot F_n
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n
            is the Set-valued presheaf of
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            regarded as an
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \hookrightarrow SSet
            = succeed "-weight" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F : X \mapsto \int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \times F(X)_n
                  \\,.
          %p
            In particular therefore for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](colim^\Delta Y_\bullet,A)
                  \\simeq
                  lim^\Delta [S^{op}, SSet](Y_\bullet,A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            With the shorthand notation introduced above the
            %strong descent condition
            finally reads, for all global-injective fibrant simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and hypercovers
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} lim^\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The right hand here is often denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Desc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, A)
                  \\,.
          %h2#descent_for_strict_groupoid_valued_presheaves
            Descent for strict
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          %p
            While simplicial sets are a very convenient model for general reasoning about higher weak categories and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty)
          %p
            Notably, by the generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              \-nerve
            injects
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} strict ∞-groupoids
            – to simplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CrsCmplx
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Str
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %mi SSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CrsCmplx \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  Str \omega Grpd \stackrel{N}{\to}
                  SSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since, for instance, something as simple as an abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (hence as an
            = succeed "-group)," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            %em
              it is desirable to have a means to control descent for simplicial presheaves which happen to factor through the
              = succeed "-nerve" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Str
                      %mi ω
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str \omega Cat
          %p In his work on descent
          %ul
            %li
              Ross Street,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical and combinatorial aspects of descent theory
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0303175"} arXiv:math.CT/0303175
          %p
            Ross Street considered presheaves with values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-categories"} strict ∞-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Str
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A : S^{op} \to Str \omega Cat
          %p
            and declared the descent
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\bullet : \Delta^{op} \to S
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mi ω
                    %mo −
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str\omega-Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim^{F \Delta} A(U^\bullet)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Str
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O := F \Delta : \Delta \to Str \omega Cat
            are the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientals"} orientals
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O = F \circ \Delta
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi Str
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : SSet \to Str\omega Cat
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} ∞-nerve
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mi Str
                    %mi ω
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : Str \omega Cat \to SSet
          %p The two prescriptions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi lim
                            %mi Δ
                          %mi N
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi U
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mi in
                          %mi SSet
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi lim
                            %mrow
                              %mi F
                              %mi Δ
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi U
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mi in
                          %mi Str
                          %mi ω
                          %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  lim^\Delta N A(U^\bullet) &amp; in SSet
                  \\\
                  \\\
                  lim^{F \Delta} A(U^\bullet) &amp; in Str \omega Grpd
                  }
          %p have a very similar appearance. The following theorem asserts if and when they are actually equivalent.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_dominic_verity Theorem (Dominic Verity)
            %p There exists a canonical comparison map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Desc
                      %mi Street
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Desc
                      %mi simp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi holim
                      %mo •
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N(Desc_{Street}(U^\bullet, A))
                    \:=
                    N(lim^{F \Delta} A(U^\bullet))
                    \\;\;\;\stackrel{\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;}{\hookrightarrow}\;\;\;
                    Desc_{simp}(U^\bullet, N \circ A)
                    \:=
                    holim_\bullet N(A(U^\bullet))
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} weak equivalence
              of
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(A(U^\bullet))
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy fibrant
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The full proof is given at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verity+on+descent+for+strict+omega-groupoid+valued+presheaves"} Verity on descent for strict omega-groupoid valued presheaves
          %h2#AsGluing Descent in terms of gluing conditions
          %p We unwrap the expression
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim^\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
          %p
            for the descent data for a presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with respect to a (hyper)cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            (whether taken in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mi ω
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str \omega Cat
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi W
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim^W\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
                  \\simeq
                  \\int^{[n] \in \Delta} [\Delta^n, A(Y_n)]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Unwrapping what this means one finds that an object/vertex of this is a choice of
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(Y_n)
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            along the maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_n \to Y_{[n-1]}
            of the
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(Y_{n-1})
          %p Namely an object in
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi W
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim^W\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
                  \\simeq
                  \\int^{[n] \in \Delta} [\Delta^n, A(Y_n)]
          %p is a commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  [2]
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  \\Delta^2 &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;
                  A(Y_2)
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  [1]
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  \\Delta^1 &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp;
                  A(Y_1)
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  [0]
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  \\Delta^0 &amp;\stackrel{a}{\to}&amp;
                  A(Y_0)
                  }
          %p
            where the vertical arrows indicate all the simplicial maps of the cosimplicial objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(Y_\bullet)
          %p So this is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_0
                an object
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A(Y_0)
            %li
              %p
                on “double intersections” (might be a cover of double intersections)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_1
                a gluing isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                        %mo *
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \pi_1^* a \to \pi_2^* a
                which identifies the two copies of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                obtained by pullback along the two projection maps
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 2
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1, \pi_2 : U \times_X U \to U
            %li
              %p
                on “triple intersections”
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_2
                a gluing 2-isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi π
                                %mn 2
                                %mo *
                              %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi π
                                    %mn 12
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi g
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ⇓
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi π
                                    %mn 23
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi g
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi π
                                %mn 1
                                %mo *
                              %mi a
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi π
                                    %mn 13
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi g
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi π
                                %mn 3
                                %mo *
                              %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; \pi_2^* a
                      \\\
                      \&amp;
                      {}^{\pi_{12}^* g}\nearrow
                      \&amp;\Downarrow^f&amp;
                      \\searrow^{\pi_{23}^* g}
                      \\\
                      \\pi_1^* a
                      \&amp;&amp;
                      \\stackrel{\pi_{13}^* g}{\to}
                      \&amp;&amp;
                      \\pi_3^* a
                      }
                which identifies the different gluing 1-isomorphisms.
          %p And so on.
          %h3#gluing_for_ordinary_stacks Gluing for ordinary stacks
          %p The article
          %ul
            %li
              Sharon Hollander,
              %em A Homotopy Theory for Stacks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0110247"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            spells out how the familiar formulation of the descent condition for ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            is equivalent to the corresponding descent condition for simplicial presheaves, discussed above.
          %h2#codescent Codescent
          %p Sometimes one wishes to compute the descent objects for presheaves of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [B(-), A] : S^{op} \to SSet
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B : S \to [S^{op}, SSet]
            is a given presheaf-valued co-presheaf. For instance in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Nonabelian+Cohomology"} differential nonabelian cohomology
            one is interested in the co-presheaf that assigns
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} fundamental ∞-groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Π
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B := \Pi : U \mapsto (V \mapsto S(V \times \Delta^\bullet, U))
          %p in which case the presheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Pi(-),A]
          %p
            would assign to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S
            the pre-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-stack of “trivial
            = succeed "-principial" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            a given (hyper)cover, the descent object for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B(-), A]
            can be expressed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Desc
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mo •
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %msup
                            %mi lim
                            %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Δ
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi colim
                            %mi Δ
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, [B(-), A])
                  \&amp; := lim^\Delta [B(Y_\bullet),A]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq \int^{[n]\in \Delta} [ \Delta^n, [B(Y_n),A] ]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq \int^{[n]\in \Delta}
                  [ \Delta^n \otimes B(Y_n), A]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq [\int_{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \otimes B(Y_n)\;,\; A ]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq [colim^\Delta B(Y_\bullet), A]
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This way the descent for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B(-),A]
            on the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = colim^\Delta U_\bullet
            is reexpressed as descent for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of the
            = succeed "-modified" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi colim
                      %mi Δ
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim^\Delta B(Y_\bullet)
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codescent"} codescent
            object, as it co-represents descent. See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-extranatural+transformation"} pseudo-extranatural transformation
          %h2#monadic_descent Monadic descent
          %p
            In some context the descent condition may algebraically be encoded in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong descent
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+descent"} cohomological descent
                %li
                  %p
